---
description: Protect the Digital Product Factory from cross-product regressions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Factory stability rules

1. Work on one product family at a time. Do not modify another generator unless
   a failing acceptance test proves that shared code requires it.
2. Before editing, run `python preflight_check.py` and record any existing
   failures. After editing, run it again. Never call work complete when it fails.
3. Tests must make zero paid API calls. Do not weaken the network guard, delete a
   failing test, change an expected result to match a defect, or accept skips.
4. Preview, Save, PDF download, and ZIP download must use the same accepted
   artifact bytes. Export must not silently regenerate a different product.
5. A QA-blocked full product must not be saved or returned as downloadable PDF.
6. Do not use unrelated vocabulary, generic placeholder text, ebook fallback,
   or test artwork to make a product appear successful.
7. Preserve Ebook, Coloring Book, Word Search, Crossword, saved projects,
   subscriptions, and exports unless they are explicitly in scope.
8. Inspect the actual downloaded PDF/ZIP for customer-path work; API success
   alone is not acceptance.
9. Keep secrets in `.env`, generated files outside Git, and make a Git checkpoint
   before approved production changes.
10. Report exact files changed, commands run, tests passed/failed, skipped test
    count, paid-call count, and any remaining blocker.
